 
<section xml:id="exercises">
  <title>Exercises</title> 
<exercise>
        <statement>
          <p>
            Consider the following system of linear equations:
            <md>
              <mrow>x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3} + x_{4} \amp= 1,</mrow>
              <mrow>x_{2} + x_{4} \amp= 1,</mrow>
              <mrow>x_{3} \amp= 1</mrow>
            </md>
          </p>
          <ol marker="(a)">
            <li><p>Write the coefficient and augmented matrix of the system.</p></li>
            <li><p>Write the system as a linear equation with vector coefficients.</p></li>
            <li><p>Write the system in matrix-vector form.</p></li>
            <li><p>Which is your favorite?</p></li>
          </ol>
        </statement>
      </exercise>

      <exercise>
        <statement>
          <p>
            Consider the matrix
            <me>A = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \amp 1 \\ 1 \amp 0\end{pmatrix}</me>
            Consider the vectors
            <me>\vec{v}_{1} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -1 \\ \end{pmatrix}, \vec{v}_{2} =\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 1 \\\end{pmatrix}</me>
          </p>
          <ol marker="(a)">
            <li><p>Compute <m>\vec{v}_{1} \cdot \vec{v}_{2}</m></p></li>
            <li><p>Compute <m>A \vec{v}_{1}</m>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Compute <m>A \vec{v}_{2}</m></p></li>
            <li><p>Compute <m>\vec{v}_{1} - A\vec{v}_{1}</m>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Describe what multiplying by <m>A</m> does in words. For which vectors <m>\vec{v}</m> does <m>A \vec{v} = \vec{v}</m>?</p></li>
          </ol>
        </statement>
      </exercise>

      <exercise>
        <statement>
          <p>
            Consider the following linear system defined by the matrix equation:
            <me>\begin{pmatrix} 1 \amp 0 \amp1 \amp 1 \\0 \amp 1 \amp 1 \amp 1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} x_{1} \\x_{2} \\x_{3}\\x_{4} \end{pmatrix} = 
            \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\0 \end{pmatrix}</me>
          </p>
          <ol marker="(a)">
            <li><p>What is the dimension of the solution set of the linear system?</p></li>
            <li><p>Solve the linear system by giving a parametric solution.</p></li>
            <li><p>Write the solution set as a span.</p></li>
            <li><p>Use your solution to give an outer representation for the plane <m>\text{span}((1,0,1,1),(0,1,1,1))</m>.</p></li>
          </ol>
        </statement>
      </exercise>

      <exercise>
        <statement>
          <p>Consider vectors <m>(1,1,0,0)</m> and <m>(0,0,1,1)</m>. Describe their span as the solution set to a system of linear equations.</p>
        </statement>
      </exercise>
</section>    
